{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0002018064","cik":"0002018064","slug":"techtarget-018064","name":"TechTarget, Inc.","ticker":"TTGT","exchanges":["Nasdaq"],"sector":"Telegraph & Other Message Communications","sic":"4822","country":"MA","website":"","listed_years":1.2,"first_annual":"2025-05-28","last_filing":"2026-07-29","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0002018064&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["TechTarget, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Telegraph & Other Message Communications\", based in MA, and has been publicly reporting for 1 year.","It reported $452.2m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 2.1% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 54.7%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($14.4m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526211990/0001193125-26-211990-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-211990"},{"text":"Gross margin of 54.7% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526211990/0001193125-26-211990-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-211990"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $14.4m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526211990/0001193125-26-211990-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-211990"},{"text":"Net cash of $47.7m against total assets of $877.9m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526211990/0001193125-26-211990-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-211990"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (1.2% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526211990/0001193125-26-211990-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-211990"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue grew only 2.1% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526211990/0001193125-26-211990-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-211990"},{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 38.8% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526211990/0001193125-26-211990-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-211990"},{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 57.5% to 54.7% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526211990/0001193125-26-211990-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-211990"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-76.3% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526211990/0001193125-26-211990-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-211990"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 7.4% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (41,815 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526271329/0001193125-26-271329-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.7% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2018064/000119312526271329/0001193125-26-271329-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 47.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.47,"consecutive":2,"current":0.547,"current_display":"54.7%","threshold_display":"47.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -13.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.13,"consecutive":2,"current":0.021,"current_display":"2.1%","threshold_display":"-13.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":0.012,"current_display":"1.2%","threshold_display":"10.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.0,"current_display":"0.00","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"